📌 SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION (SRS)
Project Name: Hospital Management System (HMS)
Version: 1.0
1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose: This document describes all functional and non-functional requirements for the Hospital Management System (HMS) Version 1.0.
The SRS provides a clear understanding of the software’s objectives to developers, testers, managers, and stakeholders.

1.2 Document Conventions
Bold text → High-priority requirements
Italic text → Optional / low-risk features
Requirement identifiers: REQ-HMS-XX

1.3 Intended Audience
Developers → For system implementation
Test Engineers → For writing test cases
Project Managers → To track requirement completion
Hospital Staff → To validate requirements

1.4 Product Scope
The HMS aims to computerize hospital operations, improve patient care, reduce delays, and maintain accurate medical records efficiently.
Main goals:
Fast patient registration, appointment scheduling, and record management
Better coordination between doctors, nurses, and admin staff
Efficient billing and pharmacy management

1.5 References
IEEE SRS guidelines
Database schema design documentation (Internal)
HL7 Healthcare Data Standards (Future scope)

2. Overall Description
2.1 Product Perspective
The HMS is a stand-alone system, extendable to integrate with:
Online appointment booking
Government health record systems
Pharmacy vendors
It replaces manual paper-based management.

2.2 Product Functions (Major modules)
Patient registration & profile management
Doctor scheduling & appointments
Electronic Medical Records (EMR)
Billing & payments
Pharmacy & inventory management
Report generation (invoices, patient medical summaries)

2.3 User Classes and Characteristics
User Type	Characteristics	Access Allowed
Admin	Technical, manages operations	Full access
Doctor	Access to patient records & diagnosis	Medical modules
Receptionist	Handles appointments & billing	Limited access
Pharmacist	Manages medicines & stock	Pharmacy module
Patient	Minimal system usage	View own reports & bills

2.4 Operating Environment
OS: Windows/Linux
Server: Apache Tomcat 9+
Database: MySQL 8+
Backend: Java 11 / Spring Boot
Browser compatibility: Chrome, Firefox, Edge

2.5 Design and Implementation Constraints
Must follow healthcare data privacy regulations
Must use Java-based technology
Must provide role-based access control

2.6 User Documentation
User manual with screenshots
Online help guide integrated into UI
FAQs for common issues

2.7 Assumptions and Dependencies
Internet connection required for email notifications
Third-party SMS gateway integration is stable and available

3. External Interface Requirements
3.1 User Interfaces
Clean UI with navbar fixed at top
Consistent layout across modules
Error messages should appear in red below fields
Reports downloadable in PDF format
3.2 Hardware Interfaces
Barcode scanner support for patient ID wristbands (future enhancement)
3.3 Software Interfaces
MySQL database via JDBC/REST API
Email/SMS APIs for notifications

3.4 Communication Interfaces
Uses HTTPS secure protocol for communication
SSL/TLS encryption enabled

4. System Features
Feature 1: Patient Management Module
Priority: High
Stimulus/Response:
User enters patient details → System stores records & generates patient ID
Functional Requirements:

REQ-HMS-01: System shall register a new patient with personal and medical data
REQ-HMS-02: System shall allow searching patients using ID or name
REQ-HMS-03: System shall maintain patient visit history
Feature 2: Appointment Scheduling
Priority: High
Doctor availability → appointment booking → confirmation
Functional Requirements:
REQ-HMS-04: System shall allow receptionists to book, update, or cancel appointments
REQ-HMS-05: System shall prevent double booking for a doctor’s time slot

Feature 3: Doctor Dashboard & EMR
Priority: High
View patient history → update diagnosis → prescribe medicines
Functional Requirements:
REQ-HMS-06: System shall allow doctors to add prescriptions & diagnosis
REQ-HMS-07: System shall store medical notes securely
Feature 4: Billing System
Priority: Medium
Auto-generate bill based on services and medicines
Functional Requirements:
REQ-HMS-08: System shall generate bills with taxes
REQ-HMS-09: System shall support multiple payment types

Feature 5: Pharmacy & Inventory
Priority: Medium
Functional Requirements:
REQ-HMS-10: System shall track stock of medicines
REQ-HMS-11: System shall alert low stock items

5. Other Non-functional Requirements
5.1 Performance Requirements
Handle 100 concurrent users
Response time < 3 seconds per request
5.2 Safety Requirements
Auto-backup database daily
Unexpected shutdown → No data loss
5.3 Security Requirements
AES-256 encryption for patient data
OTP verification for password reset
Role-based access control
5.4 Software Quality Attributes
Quality	Requirement
Usability	Simple UI with tooltips
Reliability	99.9% uptime
Availability	System operational 24/7
Maintainability	Modular code using MVC
Scalability	Vertical & horizontal scaling supported
5.5 Business Rules
Only authorized doctors can edit medical records
Medicine cannot be issued without valid prescription

